<title>UK: UK output prices up 0.2 pct in October.</title>
<headline>UK output prices up 0.2 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in October. (Prev data in brackets)</p>
<p> OUTPUT PRICES (unadj)	   OCTOBER   SEPT   (PREL SEPT)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.2	 0.3	 (0.4)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			2.3	 2.2	  (2.2)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 124.2     124.0     (124.0)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    UNCH	0.1	  (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.9	 0.9	  (0.9)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 119.8     119.8     (119.8)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX-FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO/PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.1	 0.1	  (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			0.9	 0.9	  (0.9)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr change		    0.1	 UNCH	(unch)</p>
<p> Qtr/qtr annual rate	     0.2	 UNCH	(unch)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 120.0     119.9     (119.9)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.3	 0.3	  (0.5)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-2.0	-3.1	(-2.7)</p>
<p> Index (base 1990)		 111.5     111.2     (111.6)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.5	 0.2	  (0.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-2.0	-3.1	(-2.9)</p>
<p> Index				 113.5	112.9     (113.1)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (unadj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.2	 0.2	  (0.3)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-5.4	-6.8	(-6.5)</p>
<p> Index				 107.0     106.8     (107.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F, D, T, P (adj)</p>
<p> Monthly change		    0.5	 UNCH	 (0.1)</p>
<p> Yr/yr change			-5.2	-6.7	(-6.5)  Index</p>
<p>					108.3	107.8     (108.1)</p>
<p> INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE   OCT M/M		 OCT Y/Y</p>
<p> Fuel				   1.8			-2.6</p>
<p> Crude oil etc			6.8			44.3</p>
<p> Metals				-0.7		     -13.2</p>
<p> Chemicals			    0.3			-4.2</p>
<p> Materials: home produced	-2.1			-4.3</p>
<p>		imported	     -0.3			-0.8</p>
<p> Other home produced	     -0.6			 0.7</p>
<p> Other imported materials	-0.7			-8.1</p>
<p>Consensus of economists forecasts was for input prices to rise a seasonally adjusted 0.1 percent in October and fall 2.2 percent year-on-year. Output prices are forecast up 0.2 percent and 2.3 percent higher year-on-year.</p>
